Command	Purpose
ping	Checks connectivity between computers.
ipconfig	Displays IP configuration.
ipconfig /all	Displays detailed network configuration.
ipconfig /release	Releases the DHCP IP address.
ipconfig /renew	Requests a new DHCP IP address.
ipconfig /flushdns	Clears the DNS cache.
getmac /v	Displays MAC addresses.
nbtstat -a	Displays NetBIOS information.
arp -a	Displays ARP table entries.
hostname	Displays the computer name.
netdiag	Performs network diagnostic tests.
netstat	Displays active TCP/IP connections.
nslookup	Checks DNS information.
pathping	Combines Ping and Tracert functionality.
route	Displays or modifies the routing table.

These are command-line exercises, not C programs.